  "name": "create-implementation-composites-and-composite-map",
  "description": "Contract `7.8.0`'s three implementation kinds through the generic change set: an `implementation_record` (a `STRUCTURE` with ordered `elements`), an `implementation_array` (a `FIXED-SIZE` `ARRAY` of one `element_type`, its sub-element named by `element_name`) and a `pointer` (a `DATA_REFERENCE` to a `target`), beside an application `record` and the mapping set that pairs it with the implementation record. No new tool, no new address form and no new scope vocabulary: the registry is derived from the contract, so the kinds are authored the way `create-data-type-alias` authored the first one.",
  "kind": "example",
